  "goodToKnow": "Der Luftdruck is air pressure: steigender, fallender Luftdruck, measured in Hektopascal (hPa). German weather reports talk of Hoch (high) and Tief (low), and since 1954 Berlin's Free University has named them; you can even buy the naming rights through the Wetterpate programme. Tyre pressure is der Reifendruck or Luftdruck der Reifen. It has no plural."
